  "label": "prop:polynomial-bar-involution",
  "kind": "proposition",
  "title": "Non-trivial bar-involution on the polynomial ring $R[X]$ via $X \\mapsto -X$: provides a concrete categorical setting where the indeterminate $X$ plays the role of the bar-anti-symmetric Hecke skein $h = q - q^{-1}$. All four ring-involution axioms proved via `Polynomial.comp` identities; the bar-symmetric subring is exactly $R[X^2]$ (even-degree polynomials).",
